1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:08,120
Dad, everyone at college was talking about AI today.

2
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:13,325
It is the same at our office. We used to learn how to

3
00:00:13,325 --> 00:00:19,544
do the work. Now they say the machine is learning to do our work.

4
00:00:20,144 --> 00:00:25,339
Well, I used it today. A customer needed a reply, and

5
00:00:25,339 --> 00:00:27,752
you were busy in a meeting.

6
00:00:29,152 --> 00:00:33,915
In one home, AI meant three different things. Rajiv

7
00:00:33,915 --> 00:00:39,127
worried about his work. Tara worried about her future.

8
00:00:39,127 --> 00:00:43,672
And Meera just wanted to make her day a little easier.

9
00:00:45,272 --> 00:00:50,611
I said, here is my menu. Make it clear and tidy, in

10
00:00:50,611 --> 00:00:56,984
Hindi and English. Then I asked it to help me reply to a customer.

11
00:00:57,584 --> 00:00:59,552
And you sent it?

12
00:01:00,152 --> 00:01:06,368
I read it first. It had turned my dal into a special Italian soup!

13
00:01:06,968 --> 00:01:11,429
And the price? It is a hundred and fifty here, but a

14
00:01:11,429 --> 00:01:13,736
hundred and twenty there.

15
00:01:14,336 --> 00:01:20,912
Good catch. That is exactly why I check before I send anything.

16
00:01:21,512 --> 00:01:25,900
It did not begin with a big discovery. Just a small

17
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:30,056
task that used up a little time every evening.

18
00:01:31,656 --> 00:01:35,880
The summary is ready. Please take a look.

19
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:41,391
But the goods cannot arrive on Friday. The warehouse

20
00:01:41,391 --> 00:01:47,288
is closed that day. It says so in the note at the bottom.

21
00:01:47,888 --> 00:01:51,688
The machine read the paperwork quickly. Rajiv

22
00:01:51,688 --> 00:01:56,063
understood the work behind the paperwork. That did not

23
00:01:56,063 --> 00:02:01,438
mean change had stopped. Part of his job was changing.

24
00:02:01,438 --> 00:02:05,101
He, too, needed to learn where to use the help, and

25
00:02:05,101 --> 00:02:07,016
where to check it.

26
00:02:08,616 --> 00:02:11,754
My greatest strength is finding the perfect solution

27
00:02:11,754 --> 00:02:14,328
to every difficult problem.

28
00:02:14,928 --> 00:02:19,176
Can you give an example of a time you solved a problem?

29
00:02:21,276 --> 00:02:27,126
Wait. That answer does not even sound like me. First,

30
00:02:27,126 --> 00:02:33,492
ask me what I have actually done. Then help me put my answer together.

31
00:02:34,092 --> 00:02:38,992
Getting an answer is not the same as understanding it.

32
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:43,480
This time, she practised instead of copying. She made

33
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:47,844
a mistake, then tried again in her own words.

34
00:02:49,444 --> 00:02:56,020
A customer wants to order twenty lunch boxes. The reply is ready.

35
00:02:56,620 --> 00:03:03,268
You have added the food. What about packing? And delivery?

36
00:03:03,868 --> 00:03:06,700
I did not mention those.

37
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:10,228
And it did not ask, either.

38
00:03:11,828 --> 00:03:16,278
Even a clearly written reply can be incomplete. When

39
00:03:16,278 --> 00:03:19,740
information is missing, AI can make the wrong

40
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:25,412
assumption. This time, they caught the mistake before sending it.

41
00:03:27,012 --> 00:03:31,509
Food is a hundred and fifty rupees per box. Packing is

42
00:03:31,509 --> 00:03:37,092
ten rupees per box. Delivery is two hundred rupees.

43
00:03:37,692 --> 00:03:43,179
Twenty boxes: three thousand. Packing: two hundred.

44
00:03:43,179 --> 00:03:47,284
Delivery: two hundred. The total is three thousand

45
00:03:47,284 --> 00:03:49,500
four hundred rupees.

46
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:53,562
And add this: if any information is missing, ask

47
00:03:53,562 --> 00:03:56,868
first. Do not guess.

48
00:03:57,468 --> 00:04:00,900
Now that sounds like my reply.

49
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:06,838
Meera supplied the details. Rajiv checked the numbers.

50
00:04:06,838 --> 00:04:11,500
Tara improved the question. The machine helped. The

51
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:14,412
responsibility stayed with them.

52
00:04:16,012 --> 00:04:20,224
There was no miracle the next day. Meera received a

53
00:04:20,224 --> 00:04:24,750
new question. Tara answered a practice question in her

54
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:30,508
own words. Rajiv asked at the office: when is the training?

55
00:04:31,308 --> 00:04:37,260
I need to understand this. Being afraid will not help.

56
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:42,160
How much will each job change? There is no single

57
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:47,360
answer for everyone. But you can start small. Choose

58
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:53,010
one task. Get some help. Check the result. Think

59
00:04:53,010 --> 00:04:57,198
carefully before sharing personal information. And if

60
00:04:57,198 --> 00:05:02,628
you do not understand something, do not simply assume it is correct.

61
00:05:04,228 --> 00:05:06,844
Teach me tomorrow, too.

62
00:05:07,444 --> 00:05:10,948
First, learn to make your own tea.

63
00:05:11,548 --> 00:05:15,388
Come on. We can learn both!

64
00:05:15,988 --> 00:05:20,550
AI is here. Now the question is: what will we ask it

65
00:05:20,550 --> 00:05:24,844
to do, and what must we understand for ourselves?
